It is useful only when 1-n*x is positive, but the statement holds for every n. -/
theorem pow_mul_one_sub_mul_le_one {x : ℚ} (hx : 0 ≤ x) (n : ℕ) :
    (1+x)^n * (1-(n : ℚ)*x) ≤ 1 := by logtwo_quiet
